Now write src/culling.js. Design:

- `getBoundingSphere(object)`: compute once, cache on `object.userData.__cullingSphere` (a THREE.Sphere). Compute by traversing geometry bounding spheres transformed to world space? "respecting world transforms" — compute the sphere from the object's geometry bounding box/sphere transformed by matrixWorld.

Simple approach: use Box3().setFromObject(object), then getBoundingSphere into a Sphere. That respects world transforms and children. Cache it on userData.

- Invalidation: document that callers should call `invalidateCullCache(object)` (exported) when the object moves; also cullStats uses same path. Test: move an object then call invalidate, expect updated visibility.

Implementation:

```js
import { Frustum, Matrix4, Box3, Sphere } from 'three';

const CACHE_KEY = '__cullingBoundingSphere';

export function invalidateCullCache(object) {
  if (object?.userData) delete object.userData[CACHE_KEY];
}

function getWorldSphere(object) {
  const cached = object.userData?.[CACHE_KEY];
  if (cached) return cached;
  const box = new Box3().setFromObject(object);
  const sphere = new Sphere();
  box.getBoundingSphere(sphere);
  Object.defineProperty(object.userData, CACHE_KEY, { value: sphere }); // or just assign
  return sphere;
}

export function visibleSet(camera, objects) {
  const frustum = buildFrustum(camera);
  const out = [];
  for (const obj of objects) {
    obj.updateWorldMatrix(true, false);
    const s = getWorldSphere(obj);
    if (frustum.intersectsSphere(s)) out.push(obj);
  }
  return out;
}

function buildFrustum(camera) {
  camera.updateMatrixWorld();
  camera.updateProjectionMatrix(); // maybe not necessary but fine
  const m = new Matrix4().multiplyMatrices(camera.projectionMatrix, camera.matrixWorldInverse);
  return new Frustum().setFromProjectionMatrix(m);
}
```

Note: camera.matrixWorldInverse — updateMatrixWorld updates matrixWorldInverse for cameras in newer three versions? Camera.updateMatrixWorld computes matrixWorldInverse yes (Camera overrides updateMatrixWorld and updates matrixWorldInverse). Good.

For huge object overlapping edge: Box3.setFromObject handles it.

One subtlety: setFromObject requires world matrices updated. Call obj.updateWorldMatrix(true, true).

Cache invalidation when moving: test will call invalidateCullCache after moving. Also maybe auto-check? Keep documented manual invalidation as spec says "call your documented invalidation".

